# SPA fallback for static hosts (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify).
#
# apps/web is a client-routed SPA: TanStack Router owns paths like
# /connect and /h/<serverId>/session/<agentId>. A static host knows
# nothing about those routes and, without this rule, serves its own 404
# for every one of them -- the app works only if you land on / and
# navigate, and breaks on reload or on any shared/bookmarked deep link.
#
# 200 (not 301/302) is deliberate: the browser must keep the requested
# URL so the router can read it on boot. A redirect would rewrite the
# address bar to / and lose the route the user actually asked for.
#
# Harmless in the daemon-served bundle: scripts/build-daemon-web-ui.mjs
# copies the Vite output wholesale, and Express never reads this file.
/*    /index.html   200
